WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.480
Get ready for a tragicomic clash of the symbiotes.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:08.280
Venom star Tom Hardy recently took to Instagram
to post cool fan art based on the classic

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:11.220
tragedy and comedy masks that date back to
Greek theater.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.380
These have a lot more tongue, though.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.240
Hardy clearly relishes playing the iconic
Marvel antihero, and the artwork makes reference

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.330
to Venom's post-credits scene, which indicated
that Venom will have his hands full in his

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.800
second outing on the big screen.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.620
In the scene, Hardy's Eddie Brock, an investigative
reporter, visits serial killer Cletus Kasady,

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.080
played by Woody Harrelson, to write a story
about him.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.920
After a brief and creepy round of niceties,
Kasady makes a statement that's equal parts

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.220
threat and promise.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:45.900
"When I get out of here, and I will, there's
gonna be carnage."

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:51.290
Brock may be a bit morally conflicted, but
Kasady created by writer David Michelinie

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:55.850
and artist Erik Larsen answered the unnerving
question of what would happen if a symbiote

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:01.170
were to take control of a truly evil person:
Carnage, a being so unbelievably malevolent

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:05.180
and dangerous that in the comics, Spidey and
Venom have been forced to team up on multiple

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.340
occasions to stop him.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.890
Harrelson's return to take on the villainous
mantle in Venom 2 was confirmed earlier this

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:15.320
year, and it's plain that Hardy is clearly
pumped for fans to witness the epic throwdown.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:20.160
Hardy captioned the image with a coded message
which, interestingly, could be read as "We

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.560
are Venom 2" as in the numeral two, or the
word "too," meaning "also."

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.030
In the comics, Kasady's symbiote was a spawn
of Venom, so there could be some interesting

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:29.940
subtext there.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:35.040
There's been widespread speculation that Venom
2 will carry an R rating, but producer Avi

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.400
Arad told Collider in 2018,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:42.240
"When you hear Carnage, the only thing you
can think of is R. But, if you know his story,

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.520
if you really know the comic, there's no R
there.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:45.960
He's a tortured soul.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:50.020
It's not about what he does [...] What you
have to show is, what is the motivation?

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.600
Was he born like that, or [is he] someone
we should feel for?

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.980
Because if you succeeding in making a villain
someone you can feel for, jackpot."

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:02.540
If Venom 2 indeed carries the same PG-13 rating
as its predecessor, this opens the door to

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:06.920
another question, especially in light of the
recent breakup and reconciliation between

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.900
Sony Pictures and Marvel Studios:

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.920
“Where's your pal, Spider-Man?

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.600
Let me guess, in Canada with your imaginary
girlfriend?"

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.220
There has been endless speculation about whether
Hardy's Venom and Tom Holland's Spider-Man,

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:24.220
who has appeared in three Marvel Studios films
and two Sony-produced, MCU-set solo vehicles,

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.500
will ever meet onscreen.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:30.200
Both actors seem quite psyched about the prospect,
and a number of involved parties have teased

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.500
that it's not only possible, but inevitable.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.060
Before the Sony/Disney kerfuffle, no less
an authority than Marvel Studios head honcho

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:42.040
Kevin Feige said that a crossover, quote,
"seems likely at some point," while making

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.500
it clear that in his mind, that ball was firmly
in Sony's court.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:51.240
After the release of the mega-hit Spider-Man:
Far From Home, director Jon Watts told ComicBookMovie.com

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:55.680
that, creatively speaking, he saw no reason
why the comic book nemeses couldn't meet up

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.120
on the big screen at some point.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:57.960
He said:

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.560
"I found Venom to be so funny and I thought
Tom Hardy was so great, I don't know that

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.220
[the two universes] are so different.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:08.260
I think you put those two Toms together and
you're going to see something pretty special."

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:12.700
While the two stars have in the past expressed
a general interest in working together, neither

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:16.820
have had anything to say about whether a Spidey/Venom
collision is officially in the works.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.700
For Hardy's part, though, he couldn't help
but throw a bit of gasoline on that flame

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:25.400
with a photo of himself dressed, well, rather
provocatively, which he posted to and then

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.800
deleted from his Instagram account last month.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:32.440
Either Hardy knows something we don't, or
he simply enjoys screwing with fans from time

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:32.940
to time.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.860
For the time being, we're going to have to
go with the latter; Holland's Spider-Man has

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:41.610
been confirmed to be appear in one more Sony-produced
solo flick and an additional Marvel Studios

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:45.230
film at this time, and it's been reported
that Venom 2 begins shooting this month with

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.000
director Andy Serkis at the helm.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.200
Whether Spidey makes an appearance or not,
though, we're pumped to see Hardy's anti-hero

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.200
face off with one of the deadliest foes in
Marvel comics.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:58.380
Sony has not yet announced a release date
for Venom 2, but the flick is expected to

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:03.380
drop in fall 2020, so we'll keep our ears
to the ground for details, and keep you informed.

